<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      The diameter of the mark's disc, everywhere the system draws it: the
      Android 12 splash icon, the pre-31 launch window and the recents card.

      112 is the lock screen's disc in `BiometricLock.tsx` and the web splash's
      in `providers.tsx`. One number, because the point of the entrance is that
      nothing about the mark changes size or place between the four pictures a
      cold start shows.
    -->
    <dimen name="contour_mark_disc">112dp</dimen>

    <!--
      The mark inside that disc: 86% of it, which is `MarkTile`'s rule and so
      what the lock screen draws one frame later.
    -->
    <dimen name="contour_mark">96dp</dimen>

    <!--
      The disc inside an adaptive icon, and the mark inside that disc.

      An adaptive icon's layers are 108dp and a launcher's mask crops them to
      at most the central 72dp — a circle on one launcher, a squircle on the
      next, a rounded square on a third. Drawing the disc at exactly that 72dp
      means a circular mask is filled edge to edge, with no ring of ground
      showing, while any other mask leaves the ground in its corners and the
      mark still reads as a circle. The shape stops being the launcher's
      decision, which is the whole point.

      86% is `MarkTile`'s rule for the mark's share of its disc.
    -->
    <dimen name="adaptive_disc">72dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="adaptive_disc_mark">62dp</dimen>
</resources>
